r7fixes5: the round-6 verifier's findings on lambda0 and the towers, re-derived; the stage-1 criterion
  R1: at X* the W_TT eigenvalues (e_phi1, e_theta, e_phi2) are [4*K*cos(s)/3, -2*K*cos(s)/3, -2*K*cos(s)/3] (exact); e2^T
      g e2 = M_22 + (4/3) K cos s for every symmetric M: True; with M = 0 the spectrum is {(4/3) K cos s, -(2/3) K cos s
      (x2), 2 chi, 0}: True; W U = 0: True; with M = w (e2 e3^T + e3 e2^T) the top eigenvalue at s = 0 is K/3 + (K^2 +
      w^2)^(1/2): True. (4/3) K >= [12.593464 +/- 2.75e-7] (certified, c >= 1.32407110621, envelope5 E1). So sup_s |m_1 +
      W_TT + chi D|_op >= 12.5933 + |m_1(X*)_22|, and m_1(X*) e2 != 0 raises the bound; with m_1 = 0 it is max(|W_TT|, 2
      |chi|) pointwise: True
  R2: the four-phase identity (exact): True; B maximised on a grid at (theta, v, s) = (0.0, 2.0, 0.7854) (floating point
      260.09797), certified there: B >= [260.09797 +/- 4.92e-6], so C_app (Frobenius) >= [16.127553 +/- 2.12e-8] for
      every m_1; the point (tau, r, v) = (v - a, a, v) lies in Omega: True; with eps1 <= 0.030768560: lambda0 (Frobenius)
      < [0.00190783 +/- 4.31e-9] (certified; round 4-5: 0.0019950). If m_1 were 0: sup_s |W + chi D|_F there = 16.8866
      (floating point): True
  R3: towers (s0, s1 at 0..-4; v1 at -1..-4), offset 1 on a root of its type at z = 4e-6: [('s0', -1, 0, 1), ('s1', -1,
      0, 1), ('v1', -2, -1, 1)] (type, exponent, root, multiplicity); at z = 0: [('s0', -2, -1, 1), ('s0', -1, 0, 1),
      ('s1', -3, -2, 1), ('s1', -2, -1, 1), ('s1', -1, 0, 1), ('v1', -2, -1, 1)]; all simple, so the offset-1 log order
      is <= 1 < 2 (E^iota_ind at offset 1, from v1): R5.2's table unchanged: True
  R4: f4_table with (lambda#, 0) added to G (its (2.2)-completion reaching 2.5099): rows and excesses unchanged (R0, R1):
      True; excesses (23, 47)
